{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_249","type":"agent_message","text":"\n\nThe SQLAlchemy 2.x modernization is complete. All 3 tests pass:\n\n**Changes implemented:**\n\n- **`app/repository.py`**: Migrated from legacy `.query()` to SQLAlchemy 2.x `select()` semantics. Removed `session.commit()` from `create_entry()` so callers manage transactions.\n\n- **`app/worker.py`**: Made transactions atomic - all changes commit at the end, with `session.rollback()` on exception to ensure failed operations don't persist partial state.\n\n- **`app/admin_cli.py`**: Fixed `dry_run=True` to call `session.rollback()` instead of `session.commit()`. Added rollback on exceptions.\n\n- **`docs/deploy/sqlalchemy2-cutover.md`**: Updated with the actual cutover changes and transaction boundary guidance."}}
